        "id": "fd_0363",
        "title": "Tropicalization Commutes with Neural Region Adjacency in the Large-Weight Limit",
        "description": "Conjecture: For a Zariski-open set of rational weight matrices of a fixed ReLU network architecture, if all weights and biases are scaled as powers of a parameter t and t -> infinity, then the adjacency graph of linear regions of the ReLU network stabilizes and becomes isomorphic to the face adjacency graph of an explicitly associated regular subdivision of a Newton polytope determined by the signed max-plus tropicalization of the network. Test: For small architectures, enumerate linear regions exactly, compute the associated tropical subdivision, and compare adjacency graphs over many generic rational parameter choices and growing t; a single generic counterexample refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would create a precise bridge between deep-network expressiveness and tropical/polyhedral geometry, enabling new lower bounds, architecture invariants, and geometric compression methods for neural networks.",
