        "id": "fd_0377",
        "title": "Arithmetic Universality in Torsion Persistence via Random Simplicial Complexes",
        "description": "Conjecture: For the Linial\u2013Meshulam random 2-complex Y(n,p) in the critical window p = c/n with fixed c > 0, the normalized prime-torsion persistence profile of H_1 and H_2 over the filtration by p converges in distribution, as n -> infinity, to a universal law independent of the filtration discretization and depending on c only through a finite set of scaling parameters; moreover, the cross-prime covariance decays exponentially in |log p - log q|. Test: Compute torsion barcodes of Y(n,p) for growing n across many primes and compare rescaled profiles/covariances against the predicted universal collapse; refute if no stable limiting law or no cross-prime decay appears. Impact: Would create a probabilistic statistical-mechanics theory of arithmetic topology, giving the first universality principle for prime-sensitive persistent homology and enabling prediction of torsion structure without exact computation.",
