        "description": "Conjecture: There exists a universal deterministic transform T from any finite filtered simplicial complex K to a finite family of p-local chain complexes {C_p(K)} indexed by primes p dividing some torsion order in H_*(K; Z), such that the collection of persistence barcodes over F_p together with a bounded amount of extension data reconstructed from T determines the full integer persistent homology module of K up to isomorphism. Test: Compute integer persistent homology for broad benchmark families, apply T, reconstruct from the prime-local data plus extension invariants, and check whether non-isomorphic integer persistence modules ever share identical reconstructed adelic signatures; a single counterexample refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would convert difficult integer persistent homology into parallel prime-local computations plus finite gluing data, yielding a new adelic architecture for topology, arithmetic TDA, and certified scalable torsion analysis.",
