        "description": "Conjecture: For every finite simplicial complex K and every homological degree i, there exists a universal constant C_i such that after one barycentric subdivision sd(K), the p-primary torsion barcode of the filtered chain complex induced by simplex dimension changes by at most C_i events for every prime p, and for all sufficiently large p the p-primary barcode is exactly unchanged. Test: Compute Smith normal form based persistence over Z on broad families of complexes before and after subdivision; confirm if barcode edits are uniformly bounded in i and vanish for large primes, or exhibit a counterexample family where the number of changed p-torsion intervals grows unboundedly. Impact: This would reveal an unexpected geometric regularity in arithmetic persistent homology, giving a subdivision-stability theorem for torsion features and enabling multiscale topological pipelines that preserve prime-sensitive information.",
