        "title": "p-adic Fractal Dimension of Cellular Automata Trace Sets",
        "description": "Conjecture: For every one-dimensional linear cellular automaton over F_p with local rule polynomial f(x) and every eventually periodic initial configuration, the set S of spacetime positions (n,t) where the cell value is nonzero has a p-adic trace zeta function Z_S(T)=exp(sum_{m>=1} N_m T^m/m), where N_m counts occupied positions modulo p^m along any fixed rational-slope window, and the abscissa of meromorphic continuation of Z_S determines the Euclidean box dimension of the visible spacetime fractal. In particular, two automata with distinct dominant poles of Z_S cannot have asymptotically equivalent trace fractal dimension. Test: Compute S and Z_S explicitly for Pascal, Rule 90, and other linear CA families; estimate box dimensions numerically from spacetime diagrams and compare against pole data of Z_S. Refute by exhibiting a family where the dominant p-adic pole is stable but the Euclidean box dimension differs, or vice versa. Impact: This would create a new bridge between p-adic analysis, symbolic dynamics, and fractal geometry, giving arithmetic invariants that predict visual complexity of discrete dynamical systems.",
