        "id": "fd_0382",
        "title": "Homological Noise Threshold for LLM-Guided Proof Search",
        "description": "Conjecture: For a fixed formal theorem corpus and prover, construct the tactic-state transition graph induced by an LLM policy with temperature parameter \u03c4, and let \u03b21(\u03c4) denote the first Betti number of the high-probability subgraph after thresholding edges by policy mass. There exists a nontrivial critical interval [\u03c41, \u03c42] such that theorem success rate is maximized when \u03b21(\u03c4) is within a bounded target band, while both lower and higher \u03b21(\u03c4) correlate with strictly worse success. Test: run controlled sweeps over \u03c4 and edge-threshold parameters on multiple theorem families, compute persistent homology of the induced search graphs, and check whether peak proof success consistently occurs in the predicted \u03b21 band rather than at monotone extremes. Refutation occurs if success is monotone in \u03b21 or if no stable band appears across corpora. Impact: would give a topological control law for exploration in automated theorem proving, linking stochastic language-model behavior to measurable geometric structure of search spaces and enabling principled adaptive decoding policies.",
