        "id": "fd_0384",
        "title": "Arithmetic Monodromy Controls Torsion Persistence Across Prime Fields",
        "description": "Conjecture: Let X be a finite simplicial complex with boundary matrices over Z and let D_k(t) be the Smith-normal-form invariant factors of the k-th boundary map along a one-parameter filtration t. For all but finitely many primes p, the barcode of H_k(X_t; F_p) is completely determined by the set of primes dividing the invariant factors D_k(t) together with the permutation action of Frobenius on the roots of the corresponding determinantal minors; moreover, two filtrations with identical integer persistence barcodes but different Frobenius cycle statistics over varying p yield distinguishable mod-p barcode distributions on a set of primes of positive density. Test: Compute integer persistence and determinantal minors for explicit filtered complexes, sample many primes p, and compare observed mod-p barcode frequencies against predictions from Frobenius conjugacy classes/Chebotarev densities. The conjecture is refuted if mod-p barcode distributions show no dependence beyond integer torsion divisibility data, or if predicted prime-density splits fail systematically. Impact: This would create a new arithmetic refinement of persistent homology, linking TDA to Galois/monodromy data and enabling prime-sensitive topological fingerprints invisible to ordinary barcodes.",
