        "title": "Prime-Sensitive Spectral Rigidity of Simplicial Complexes",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an infinite family of finite simplicial complexes {K_n} with uniformly bounded dimension and degree such that the full real Laplacian spectrum of each K_n is identical, but the multiset of H_1(K_n; F_p) barcode lengths under a canonical filtration differs for infinitely many primes p; moreover, these prime-dependent barcode differences cannot be recovered from any finite collection of real or complex spectral invariants of the filtered Hodge Laplacians. Test: Construct candidate isospectral filtered complexes computationally, compute persistent homology over F_p across many primes, and check whether barcode discrepancies persist despite matching spectra at every filtration level over R. Refutation occurs if prime-dependent persistence is always determined by sufficiently rich spectral data. Impact: This would reveal a fundamentally arithmetic layer of topological data invisible to classical spectral geometry, motivating new prime-aware invariants for TDA, geometry, and scientific data analysis.",
